### The lid-driven cavity at Re = 100, the standard first test of a
### flow PINN.  Two inputs, three field components, three residuals:
###
###   R1  u_x + v_y                                        = 0
###   R2  u u_x + v u_y + p_x - nu ( u_xx + u_yy )          = 0
###   R3  u v_x + v v_y + p_y - nu ( v_xx + v_yy )          = 0
###
### with nu = U L / Re = 0.01 and rho = 1.  The advection terms multiply
### one component by the derivative of another, which is what the System
### block exists for.
###
### The boundary condition prescribes u and v on the four walls and says
### nothing about the pressure, so Sys_wcomp gives the pressure a weight
### of zero in the supervised term.  Fitting it to a boundary value it
### does not have would over-constrain the problem; the pressure is
### determined by the momentum equations up to a constant, which is all
### the physics fixes.
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260820 /
Restart      0 /
Output_deriv 0 /

Nlayer       5 /
2 / (x, y)
40 /
40 /
40 /
3 / (u, v, p)

Loss_term  DATA         1000  data.dat    1.d0  /
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  4000  colloc.dat  1.d-2 /

Sys_wcomp  1.d0 1.d0 0.d0 /   the wall data says nothing about p

System 3 12 /
TRM  1  1   1 0   1.d0    /   u_x
TRM  1  2   0 1   1.d0    /   v_y
XUX  2  1 1 1 0   1.d0    /   u * u_x
XUX  2  2 1 0 1   1.d0    /   v * u_y
TRM  2  3   1 0   1.d0    /   p_x  (rho = 1)
TRM  2  1   2 0  -1.d-2   /   -nu u_xx
TRM  2  1   0 2  -1.d-2   /   -nu u_yy
XUX  3  1 2 1 0   1.d0    /   u * v_x
XUX  3  2 2 0 1   1.d0    /   v * v_y
TRM  3  3   0 1   1.d0    /   p_y
TRM  3  2   2 0  -1.d-2   /   -nu v_xx
TRM  3  2   0 2  -1.d-2   /   -nu v_yy

Hod_K      2 /
1.d0
0.d0
0.d0
Hod_dense  1 /

Hod_check  0 /
Num_validation 200 /
Validation_cyc 100 /
P_max          20000 /
Epoch      2000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-14 /
Num_batch  100 /
Checkpoint_cyc 100000 /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.002d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
